  {
    result: "Essential repeat (failed three or more main subjects)",
    means: "In the Delhi High Court case, a student who failed three of five main theory subjects was placed in Essential Repeat and could not take the supplementary exam.",
    next: "Repeat the year in your school, appear as a private candidate where the board allows it, or move to NIOS.",
  },
  {
    result: "Passed theory but failed practical or internal marks",
    means: "The court read CBSE bye-law 40.1 to mean 33 percent in theory and 33 percent in practical or internal assessment are needed separately. A good internal grade alone does not give a pass certificate.",
    next: "Ask your school exactly which component you failed, and ask whether the supplementary exam covers it.",
  },
  {
    result: "State board result (PUC, Intermediate, Plus Two, HSC)",
    means: "State boards run their own supplementary exams. The name, dates and number of subjects differ, so the CBSE rules above do not carry over.",
    next: "Read your own board's circular. Tamil Nadu officials, for example, said in 2023 that tens of thousands of failed students did not apply for the supplementary test.",
  },
];

const fourRoutes = [
  {
    n: "A",
    title: "Clear the subject and keep the degree route",
    body: "Best when you failed one or two subjects. The supplementary exam is the quickest way back, and your marks are usually good in the rest.",
  },
  {
    n: "B",
    title: "Move to NIOS and clear it at your pace",
