    a: "Yes, in some cases. The NIOS FAQ says learners from other boards can transfer up to two subjects passed in the last five years, if those subjects are in the NIOS scheme. You must ask at the time of admission, with the original marksheet.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can I do a degree without passing Class 12?",
    a: "Some open-university bridge programmes exist. A study-centre listing for IGNOU's Bachelor's Preparatory Programme says it has no formal qualification requirement, a minimum age of 18, and a duration of six months to two years. Confirm the current rules with IGNOU before you rely on it.",
  },
  {
    q: "What jobs can I get after failing Class 12?",
    a: "Retail, hospitality, sales, delivery, data entry and trade apprenticeships are common starting points, and skilled work in design, digital marketing and software can follow with proof. Pay at the start is modest, so pair the job with a skill project.",
  },
